SDL 3.4.18's test/testautomation*.c, made to compile as C++ (C++23), so that
tools/run_conformance.py can build them against `import mcpplibs.mwrap.sdl3;`
instead of <SDL3/SDL.h>. Applied with `git apply` to a copy in target/; the
repository never holds upstream's test sources. Each change is what C++
requires of C and nothing else:

  - void * converted implicitly (SDL_malloc, SDL_GetClipboardData, userdata,
    surface->pixels): an explicit cast to the pointer type;
  - an int or Uint32 stored in an enum (SDL_AudioFormat, SDL_PixelFormat,
    SDL_IOWhence, the stdio SEEK_END): an explicit cast, or the array typed as
    the enum (testautomation_surface.c);
  - a string literal passed as void * (SDL_SetPointerProperty): a cast;
  - a function pointer passed as void * (SDL_PROP_IOSTREAM_MEMORY_FREE_FUNC_POINTER):
    a cast;
  - SDL_SECONDS_TO_NS(negative) + n, an unsigned value, initialising an
    SDL_Time in a braced list (narrowing): a cast, as C converts it;
  - a goto that crosses two initialised declarations (testautomation_video.c):
    the declarations without initialisers, then assignments;
  - "%"SIZE_FORMAT (a user-defined-literal suffix in C++11): a space.

